BSD cubed (BSD Desktop Daemon, bsddd) is an experimental C compatibility
bridge between desktop session interfaces and native FreeBSD services.
This version provides ConsoleKit session discovery, authenticated controller
lifetime management, selected sd-login functions, and partial login1 objects.

It does not yet enable a native GNOME Wayland session. Device handoff,
seat lifecycle and modern GNOME session startup remain in development.
No systemd implementation, D-Bus policy or boot service is installed.
